From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:21:25 +0000
Subject: cpufreq: cppc: no energy model without PEFG, drop the cooling flag

Firmware without \_SB.PMMX.PEFG has no CPU power data. Skip the energy
model with one info message instead of an error for each policy.

CPUFREQ_IS_COOLING_DEV registers through of_cpufreq_cooling_register(),
which needs a DT CPU node. CPPC is ACPI only, so the call always fails.
CPU cooling under ACPI comes from the processor driver.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/cppc_cpufreq.c | 12 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/cppc_cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/cppc_cpufreq.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cppc_cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cppc_cpufreq.c
@@ -756,6 +756,12 @@ static int cppc_opp_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* Firmware without PEFG has no power data: no energy model. */
+	if (!acpi_has_method(NULL, "\\_SB.PMMX.PEFG")) {
+		pr_info_once("No \\_SB.PMMX.PEFG, CPU energy model disabled\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	do {
 		struct acpi_buffer buffer = { ACPI_ALLOCATE_BUFFER, NULL };
 		union acpi_object *package;
@@ -1254,11 +1260,7 @@ static struct freq_attr *cppc_cpufreq_attr[] = {
 };
 
 static struct cpufreq_driver cppc_cpufreq_driver = {
-	.flags = CPUFREQ_CONST_LOOPS | CPUFREQ_NEED_UPDATE_LIMITS
-#ifdef CONFIG_CIX_THERMAL
-		 | CPUFREQ_IS_COOLING_DEV
-#endif
-		 ,
+	.flags = CPUFREQ_CONST_LOOPS | CPUFREQ_NEED_UPDATE_LIMITS,
 	.verify = cppc_verify_policy,
 	.target = cppc_cpufreq_set_target,
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_CIX
-- 
